  "live_records": {
    "q-1802": {
      "dom_id": "step-q1802",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{3}).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{3})$ means the same thing as ${}_{7}{C}_{3}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=7$ and $r=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{7}{C}_{3} & =\\frac{7!}{(7-3)!3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7!}{4!3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5}{6} \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
