    "q-84993": {
      "dom_id": "step-q84993",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Evaluate $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{25}{0}).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{25}{0})$ means the same thing as ${}_{25}{C}_{0}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=25$ and $r=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{25}{C}_{0} & =\\frac{25!}{(25-0)!0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{25!}{25!0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{25!}}{\\cancel{25!}\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
